<http://data.silknow.org/object/32999148-3874-3c48-b2e3-3b74017692f4>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Ladies cap, English, ca. 1860 - ca. 1865"@en , "Ladies cap. A white tatted triangular 'manchon' is mounted onto a black net cap shaped to the head, and gathered at the back of the neck. Across the brow is a band composed of gathered tatting, trimmed with rosettes of narrow purple ribbon with white borders, and purple silk ribbon, to which are attached the cap ribbons, purple silk, and tatted borders."@en ;
